5yzc|a|A sort of ecclesiastical heriot, a customary gift claimed by, and due to, the minister of a parish on the death of a parishioner. It seems to have been originally a voluntary bequest or donation, intended to make amends for any failure in the payment of tithes of which the deceased had been guilty. ; A burial place; a place for the dead. ; A place for the reception of the dead before burial; a deadhouse; a morgue. ; Of or pertaining to the dead; as, mortuary monuments.	j:9hai,115,10;1pyf,52,3~9hai,115,10;1pyf,52,3
